	(text "left key board, generated by tools/sch_keys.py from layout/keys.json (36 switches, 36 LEDs). Diode anode to the switch (column side), cathode on the row net. LED rail +5V_LED is switched by the TPS22918 (expander LED_EN, 100k pull-down).\nLED_CT 1n: about 2.5 ms rise, inrush about 0.2 A into the rail's bulk. 220 R in front of the first LED (DIN must not exceed the LED rail by 0.5 V when the rail is off).\nMatrix diodes are Schottky: a 1N4148 at 0.3 mA leaves the column above the expander's 0.2 VDD input-low limit. INTA of every chip is wired to INT (firmware sets open drain before enabling interrupts; pull-up on the port board); INTB unused."
